        {
          "id": 1964289562,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "There is a separate elcid field (mac-lte.sch.elcid) that gets added regardless, which is set to be the 6 bits+32.  So for those fields, its the index (+32) rather than the codepoint that gets set as the value as \"elcid\".\n\nAre you suggesting that a single LCID field should also always be set to the codepoint value?  For \"Extended locical channel ID field\", it would potentially be logged twice (i.e. as 32 and as elcid-bits + 32).  If we do this, I wonder whether having the elcid field have the +32 in it is really what we want?\n\nI don't think mac-nr is done in an ideal way either - where there are 2 EXT LCIDs and different amounts offsets to their codepoint values...",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
